Given differential equation is,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}=\sqrt[3]{1+\left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^{2}} \\
\Rightarrow\left(\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}\right)^{3}=1+\left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^{2}
\end{array}
\]<br>Order \( =2 \) and degree \( =3 \)

Given differential equation is,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
x \frac{d y}{d x}-y=3 \\
\Rightarrow x \frac{d y}{d x}=3+y \\
\Rightarrow \frac{d y}{3+y}=\frac{d x}{x}
\end{array}
\]<br>Integrating both the sides, we have<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\int \frac{d y}{3+y}=\int \frac{d x}{x} \\
\Rightarrow \ln (3+y)=\ln x+\ln c \\
\Rightarrow(3+y)=c x
\end{array}
\]<br>The equation is a straight line equation.

Given differential equation,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\frac{d y}{d x}+y=\frac{1+y}{x} \\
\Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}+y\left(1-\frac{1}{x}\right)=\frac{1}{x}
\end{array}
\]<br>So, integrating factor is given by<br>I.F. \( =e^{\int\left(1-\frac{1}{x}\right) d x}=e^{x} e^{-\ln x}=\frac{e^{x}}{x} \)

Given differential equation,<br>\[
\left[1+\left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^{2}\right]^{2}=\frac{d^{2} y}{d x}
\]<br>The given differential equation has order \( 2 \) and degree \( 1 \).

Given differential equation is,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
x \frac{d y}{d x}-y=x^{4}-3 x \\
\Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}-\frac{1}{x} y=x^{3}-3
\end{array}
\]<br>General differential equation of this type is given by<br>\( \frac{d y}{d x}+P(x) y=Q(x) \)<br>Here \( P=-\frac{1}{x} \) and \( Q=x^{3}-3 \) So, I.F. factor is given by,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\text { I.F. }=e^{\int P d x}=e^{\int-\frac{1}{x} d x} \\
=e^{-\log x}=e^{\log \left(\frac{1}{x}\right)}=\frac{1}{x}
\end{array}
\]

